RF.put("questb:b51",{"8691":{"id":8691,"t":"Drape of Vaulted Secrets","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Martial Drape, 2 Alabaster Idols, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Keyl Swiftclaw in Silithus. You must also obtain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Martial Drape General Rajaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Kurinnaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Alabaster Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"I'm glad to hear you're aiding us in our attack on Ahn'Qiraj, ‹name›. I can make you a protective item that'll be of assistance in the fight against our enemy, ‹class›.\nI shall need a Qiraji drape, which I'll resize for you of course. I'll also need idols and scarabs which I'll use to create a suitable clasp.\nI promise you won't be disappointed.","rew":"You will receive:\nDrape of Vaulted Secrets\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring the materials for the cloak, ‹name›?","done":"Ah yes... this drape is immaculate.\nTake this cloak, ‹name›. May it protect you from the foul magic of the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Keyl Swiftclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8851":{"id":8851,"t":"Five Signets for War Supplies","lv":19,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Horde Commendation Signet","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.8,"y":67.3,"n":"Warlord Gorchuk","s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8611":{"id":8611,"t":"The Horde Needs Lean Wolf Steaks!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 49.","obj":"Bring 20 Lean Wolf Steaks to Bloodguard Rawtar at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Lean Wolf Steak","desc":"I'm not standing here just to get a nice tan, ‹class›. There are war preparations to be made. If we're going to crush those bugs at Ahn'Qiraj then we need to be ready, and that includes food too!\nThey have me gathering and salting lean wolf steaks here for the upcoming war. But since I need to stay here to take care of all of this, I need you to go out, kill some wolves and then cook up the meat into lean wolf steaks and bring them back to me here. You got all that?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"The sprite darters can be dangerous critters when provoked. Be careful when dealing with them, ‹class›. And be even more careful of any night elves in the area. The pestering fools tend to hold up in the forests also.\nWhen you've gotten enough of the wings, let me know, I'll be sure to reward you well!","done":"Wonderful, ‹class›! These will do nicely. There are enough here to make a cloak for Korrin, and possibly even more! Thank you.\nI hope the trip wasn't too dangerous? The area of Feralas is not known for being forgiving, but you've obviously done well enough.\nThank you again, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":28.8,"y":67.4,"n":"Bloodguard Rawtar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"7171":{"id":7171,"t":"Legendary Heroes","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Insignia Rank 4","desc":"Your radiate command and power, shaman. Exalted in the eyes of Frostwolf - the enemy cowers at the mention of your name.\nRise, Hero of Frostwolf. Rise and be honored!\nPresent your insignia.","rew":"You will receive:\nStormpike Insignia Rank 5\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+200 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Before me stands an exalted hero of the Alliance.\n<Lieutenant Haggerdin salutes.>\nFew have earned such a rank among the Stormpike. I have watched the enemy fall before you. I have seen their resolve crumble in your presence. When you enter the fray, you become the beacon of hope for our forces!\nPresent your insignia.","done":"Surely it will be you who carries the Eye of Command!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Lieutenant Haggerdin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"691":{"id":691,"t":"Worth Its Weight in Gold","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find 10 Witherbark Tusks, 4 Witherbark Medicine Pouches and a Shadow Hunter Knife for Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe.\n10 Witherbark Tusk Witherbark Axe Thrower 37 % , Witherbark Troll 37 % , Witherbark Headhunter 28 % , Witherbark Witch Doctor 25 % and 4 more\n4 Witherbark Medicine Pouch Witherbark Witch Doctor 33 %\nShadow Hunter Knife Witherbark Shadow Hunter 20 %","desc":"Archmage Malin sent Skuerto and I here to collect reagents for him. I was at a loss as to how I was going to collect the items, but now that you're here, I think my problem's solved.\nI need the following: Witherbark tusks, Witherbark medicine pouches and a shadow hunter knife.\nCould you find those for me? The Witherbark live to the southeast of Arathi.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,500\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you had any luck so far, ‹name›?\n<Kryten makes some notes in his journal as he reads.>\nIf my research is correct, the tusks should come from any Witherbark troll. The medicine pouches come from the Witherbark witch doctors, and the strongest of the Witherbark shadow hunters should carry the special knife given to them after they've completed their rites of passage. There's no way to tell which shadow hunters will have the knife until you do battle.","done":"Incredible! I can see why Malin asked you to come join us - very well done indeed!\nAt this rate, Skuerto and I will be headed back to Stormwind in no time at all.\nI believe my dwarven companion is back from scouting Boulderfist Hall; go speak to him when you're ready.\nIt looked as though he might have had a bit of a scuffle with the ogres. Don't mention that to him, though; he's very sensitive about criticisms to his skills at scouting.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46.2,"y":47.8,"n":"Apprentice Kryten","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1011":{"id":1011,"t":"Forsaken Diseases","lv":29,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Bottle of Disease to Kayneth Stillwind in Forest Song.\nBottle of Disease Bottle of Disease","desc":"The Forsaken, the undead arm of the Horde, have crept into Ashenvale, lurking at our ruins and our barrows. We believe their goal is to spread disease amongst the lands of the night elves. We must confirm this!\nThe Forsaken have a camp south of here, near the Dor'Danil Barrow Den, where they create poisons and diseases and place them in bottles. Fight your way into that camp and steal a bottle of disease. Return with such a bottle. I will test it and find its purpose.","rew":"Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Did you find the camp, ‹name›? Do you have a bottle of disease?","done":"Very good, ‹name›. Now... by testing the contents of this bottle, the goals of the Forsaken will be revealed!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":85.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Kayneth Stillwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"2771":{"id":2771,"t":"A Good Head On Your Shoulders","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring two Mithril Coifs and one Ornate Mithril Shoulder to Trenton Lighthammer.\n2 Mithril Coif\nOrnate Mithril Shoulders","desc":"It seems as if master had this planned from the start. I was not taught to create the items which you learned to create and you were not taught the items which I learned to create.\nThe master is wise, ‹name›. We shall teach each other!\nShow me how to make a mithril coif and ornate mithril shoulders and I shall show you how to create an ornate mithril helm.","rew":"You will learn: Ornate Mithril Helm\nExperience: 3,900","back":"Have you completed the crafting of the items, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent! A fair tradeoff, if I do say so myself. Watch and learn, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.8,"n":"Trenton Lighthammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"7651":{"id":7651,"t":"Enchanted Thorium Platemail: Volume III","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 55. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 14,500, 0.46 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nEnchanted Thorium Platemail\nProvided: Enchanted Thorium Platemail","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Enchanted Thorium Helm\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Well done, my boy.\n<Lorekeeper Lydros tears out a page from the book.>\nI am sure you can make use of this recipe.\nStart an item: Enchanted Thorium Platemail End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 56 58 Side Both factions Type Dungeon Profession Blacksmithing 300 Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7651","cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97971":{"id":97971,"t":"Camping 101 skinning","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Mendalass Tattermend in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your skinning skill to 20","desc":"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.2,"y":43.4,"n":"Mendalass Tattermend","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"6611":{"id":6611,"t":"To Gadgetzan You Go!","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak with Dirge Quikcleave about advancing your cooking career.","desc":"How you expect Zamja teach you anything? You got all of Zamja's cooking mojo and still you crave more!\nZamja can't help. Fat ‹race› needs to go to Gadgetzan. You find a little goblin named Dirge there - he help you, fatty.\nWhen you become big cook on the block, you come back and teach Zamja, ok? Now go!","rew":"Experience: 975","done":"<Dirge spits out some leather sandal bits.>\nPfftooey...\n<Dirge hacks loudly.>\nWhat? I'll have you know that leather is surprisingly high in protein and low in carbohydrates.\nOrgrimmar Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":57.4,"y":54,"n":"Zamja","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.6,"y":28.1,"n":"Dirge Quikcleave","e":1}],"cats":["cooking"]},"94291":{"id":94291,"t":"Craftsmans writ dark iron bomb","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Dark Iron Bomb\nDark Iron Bomb","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Dark Iron Bomb, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Dark Iron Bomb Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94291","cats":["crafting"]},"7891":{"id":7891,"t":"Green Iron Bracers","lv":60,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Green Iron Bracers","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"I'm working on a new costume, for when I have my own booth as the strongest woman alive! Right now I'm looking for some bracers I can wear. They can't cover much because people want to see my muscles, but I still want to flash a little color, you know?\nHow about green iron bracers, ‹name›? Can you make me green iron bracers? If you can, then I have a whole bunch of Darkmoon Faire tickets for you.","done":"Thanks much, ‹name›. Here's your Darkmoon Faire tickets!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.6,"y":46.4,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.5,"y":69.9,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"5091":{"id":5091,"t":"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!","lv":50,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist. His base camp is located at Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains.","desc":"Hear ye, hear ye! All heroes are called upon to heed these words!\nA call to arms has been issued by the Kingdom of Stormwind! All able bodied individuals are entreated to take up arms against the dark threat of the Scourge in the northern lands of the Eastern Kingdoms! Rumors fly of new threats rising from the ruins of the Plaguelands!\nHeroes of the realm - seek out Commander Ashlam Valorfist who has set up his base camp in Chillwind Camp, north of the Alterac Mountains!","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Welcome to the Plaguelands, hero. This is one of the most dangerous frontiers in Azeroth, especially with the looming threat of the Scourge to our north and northeast. I am glad to hear that the clarion call of duty and service to the greater good did not fall on deaf ears with you!\nIf you are ready to get your hands dirty, then there is plenty for willing and able heroes to do here on the edge of the Plaguelands.\nDarnassus Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":47.8,"y":82,"n":"Herald Moonstalker","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"291":{"id":291,"t":"The Reports","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Senir's report to Senator Barin Redstone in Ironforge.\nSenir's Report\nProvided: Senir's Report","desc":"Excellent! Take my report to Senator Barin Redstone. He's a sour type, so don't let his less-than-sunny disposition get to you. He's in Ironforge, in the chamber where King Magni holds court.\nDon't know the way to Ironforge? Take the road out of Kharanos north, cross the bridge, then follow the road east--there are large banners flanking the road--up the mountainside.\nBy the way, if you might avoid mentioning how you assisted me? Can't let them think I'm not working hard out here, you know?","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Ironforge\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Hmm... it would seem that my guards are becoming less discriminatory with petitioners. Well, what do you want? Make it quick.","done":"<He quickly peruses the report.>\nAuthority of the KING!? Has Magni taken complete leave of his senses! And that damnable Whitebeard... Taken matters into his own hands, has he? The Senate will not be pleased to hear about this, not one bit.\nWhat, are you still here? Go, before I call the guards!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.7,"y":53.8,"n":"Senir Whitebeard","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.3,"n":"Senator Barin Redstone","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"1251":{"id":1251,"t":"The Black Shield","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Blackened Iron Shield to Krog in Brackenwall Village.\nBlackened Iron Shield\nProvided: Blackened Iron Shield","desc":"An iron shield, blackened by the fire that raged through the inn, is affixed to the crumbling chimney, one of the few remaining parts of the structure that once made up the Shady Rest Inn.\nThe shield can be removed from the brick of the chimney.","rew":"Experience: 700","back":"What's that you have there, ‹name›? Evidence from the remains of the Shady Rest Inn?","done":"I grant that humans have strange decorating tastes, but would they use a plain iron shield to adorn their fireplace? Perhaps this shield was placed there by the ones who burned the inn.\nA warning? A threat?","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":29.6,"y":48.6,"n":"Black Shield","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.4,"y":31.9,"n":"Krog","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"1171":{"id":1171,"t":"The Brood of Onyxia","lv":43,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village.","desc":"You leave me alone now. Go tell Draz'Zilb we stay here. No black dragon here.","rew":"Experience: 360","done":"That lazy coward!\nMok'Morokk displayed strength when Rexxar was our leader. But soon after Rexxar's departure Mok'Morokk fell prey to temptations of power. Rather than lead, he demanded. He does not serve his people but rather expects us to serve him.\nSomething must be done.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.3,"y":31.4,"n":"Overlord Mok'Morokk","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":37.2,"y":33.1,"n":"Draz'Zilb","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"6131":{"id":6131,"t":"Timbermaw ally","lv":48,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Grazle wants you to prove yourself by killing 5 Deadwood Warriors, 5 Deadwood Pathfinders, and 5 Deadwood Gardeners.\nDeadwood Warrior slain : 0/ 5\nDeadwood Pathfinder slain : 0/ 5\nDeadwood Gardener slain : 0/ 5","desc":"The Timbermaw are the only furbolg tribe to escape the corruption. However, many other races kill furbolg blindly now, without bothering to see if they are friend or foe. For this reason, the Timbermaw furbolg trust very few.\nAre you interested in proving yourself? Drive back the corrupted Deadwood tribe of Felwood and we may one day consider you an ally. You'll find the first Deadwood tribe - warriors, pathfinders and gardeners - to my west.\nFelwood Open the zone on the world map Level 48 , requires level 45 Difficulty 45 46 51 60 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 6131","cats":["felwood"]},"5891":{"id":5891,"t":"Salve via Disenchanting","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Lesser Nether Essence","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. I've devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. You don't need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work.\nI just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!","done":"Here are some Cenarion plant salves - I only need one lesser nether essence for this, ‹name›. Essence is by far the most potent item I can make use of to turn swords into plowshares, as it were. If you need more salve, then find me here!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4131":{"id":4131,"t":"The Woodpaw Gnolls","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search the Woodpaw Gnoll camps of southern Feralas for evidence of the courier's belongings or the courier himself.","desc":"Our \"friends\" the Woodpaw might have gotten Raschal in the end, but something tells me that's not what occurred. Still, they're the best place to start looking.\nI wish I had clearer insight as to what to do, but all I have right now is 'Search the Woodpaw camps - go.' I do know that gnolls will keep items they scavenge and fight over them; maybe they ran across the backpacks Quint mentioned. I hadn't risked a head-on fight in past searches, but with Quint's vision on this I say rip into them.","rew":"Experience: 2,800\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Tacked up on a nearby tree are two large leather backpacks. Each bears a small insignia of the Feathermoon Stronghold on the front of the pack...","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31.9,"y":45.1,"n":"Ginro Hearthkindle","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":73.3,"y":56.3,"n":"Large Leather Backpacks","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"7731":{"id":7731,"t":"Stinglasher","lv":47,"min":39,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat Stinglasher in the Writhing Deep, bringing its glands back to Hadoken Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache, Feralas.\nStinglasher's Glands Stinglasher","desc":"In surveying the Writhing Deep, one of our scouts reported seeing a giant insect - much larger than the other insects spotted - wandering about the twisted terrain. Not only is it larger, it also seems to secrete some sort of aura that the other insects don't. We've given it a name - Stinglasher.\nThe innards of this beast would be invaluable to study as we figure out the best way to deal with this new threat. Cut out its secretion glands and bring it back to me immediately!","rew":"Money: 1 35 1 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,200\n+150 reputation with Horde","back":"Have you managed to bring down Stinglasher yet?","done":"Impressive, ‹class›... most impressive! If Stinglasher is indeed one of their strongest creatures, the study of the beast will prove to be quite valuable in time. It's now my charge to make sure we defend ourselves long enough to take advantage of it.\nPlease accept this coin bounty as a token of the entire camp's thanks, ‹name›. Well done.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.9,"y":42.5,"n":"Hadoken Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2931":{"id":2931,"t":"Castpipe's Task","lv":28,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge.","desc":"Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge has need of adventurers! He's organizing bands to reenter Gnomeregan on a data retrieval mission of top security and importance.\nCastpipe might not be a member of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences like I am, but he's still a smart gnome so if he thinks it's important, then by my calculations there's an eighty-four percent probability that it really is important!\nThose are good odds!","rew":"Experience: 230\n+10 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"I'm organizing data extraction missions into Gnomeregan. If you're here for that, then listen up!\nStonetalon Mountains Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":28.8,"n":"Master Mechanic Castpipe","e":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"7811":{"id":7811,"t":"A Donation of Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"‹name›, you've been a tremendous contributor to our cloth drive. As we work hard to replenish our reserves, one form of cloth remains critically low - runecloth. We are in absolutely dire need of runecloth, and we hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past.\nIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We'll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we'll go from there.","done":"Fantastic - these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We'd certainly be lost without you.\nWith all the donations you've made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future. Just be sure to check in with me, and I'll personally make sure that your good deeds won't go unrecognized!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":28.8,"n":"Bubulo Acerbus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8371":{"id":8371,"t":"Concerted Efforts","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor, 3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor and 3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"We're not fighting isolated battles against the Horde anymore, lad/lass.\nVictory in one front means denying the Horde resources they'd use against us in a different battle. By the same token, losing any given battle could give the advantage to our opponent somewhere else around the world.\nThe Alliance is in need of more combatants with this sort of worldly understanding... truly seasoned veterans! ‹name›, come back to me after you've served against the Horde at all of our active battlegrounds.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with The League of Arathor\n+200 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+150 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"How are yer travels faring laddie?","done":"You're not one to disappoint, ‹name›! What you've learned goes beyond petty medals and commendations. What you've learned is what can only come with experience and the hardening of one's temper in the field of battle.\nYou've done well, ‹class›. You're a true hero of the Alliance!\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8931":{"id":8931,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Beaststalker's Belt and a set of Beaststalker's Gloves to Deliana in Ironforge.\nBeaststalker's Belt Smolderthorn Headhunter 4.2 % , Rage Talon Dragon Guard 3.8 % , Firebrand Legionnaire 3.1 % , Bloodaxe Raider 2.7 % and 2 more\nBeaststalker's Gloves War Master Voone 0 %","desc":"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me an ordinary belt and a set of gloves that you wish to upgrade.","rew":"You will receive:\nBeastmaster's Belt Beastmaster's Gloves\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the trade?","done":"You've kept your end of the bargain, I shall keep mine.\nJust remember that I'm holding on to the best pieces until your work is finished.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2851":{"id":2851,"t":"Wild Leather Boots","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Nightscape Pants, 2 Nightscape Boots, and 2 Wildvines to Pratt McGrubben in Feathermoon Stronghold.\n2 Nightscape Pants\n2 Nightscape Boots\n2 Wildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"You've learned quite a bit now, ‹name›; still, there is more for you to learn. Next are Wild Leather boots, the cornerstone of any set.\nThese boots are crafted to cradle the foot in comfort while bracing it against the hazards of adventuring. The soft soles are a blessing to those seeking quiet movement in footwear.\nFor this pattern, I need an order of two Nightscape pants and two Nightscape boots filled. I also will require two wildvines... not just one. When you have all this, let me know.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Boots\nExperience: 2,900","back":"The order on the pants, boots, and wildvines needs to be filled before you get the pattern, ‹name›. Are you finished?\nFrom the earliest pair of boots we learn how to make, we start to understand that a quality boot needs to ride a razor's edge between comfort and function. With both, we are able to create items that allow the wearer to ignore fatigue that would cripple those wearing lower quality goods.","done":"Once again, you've filled a complex order with the skill of a seasoned professional. You have earned this pattern, as well as my thanks.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"9251":{"id":9251,"t":"Atiesh, the Befouled Greatstaff","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Anachronos at the Caverns of Time in Tanaris wants the Staff Head of Atiesh and the Base of Atiesh.\nStaff Head of Atiesh Kel'Thuzad in Naxxramas\nBase of Atiesh C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple","desc":"You question why you are still alive. After all, you have in your possession an item of great evil. The answer is not clear, ‹name›. I only do as I must.\nKel'Thuzad sits atop his throne in Naxxramas, plotting... He seeks that which you hold and holds that which you seek.\nAs for the base of the staff; the dwarf, Brann Bronzebeard, held it when he entered Ahn'Qiraj. He has left Ahn'Qiraj but the base of Atiesh remains.\nShould you succeed in recovering the pieces, return them to me.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"In its current form, the staff is far too dangerous to be in the hands of a mortal.","done":"There is a being within... a being not of this world.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["legendary"]},"531":{"id":531,"t":"Vyrin's Revenge","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Hunting Satchel.","obj":"Bring Ol' Sooty's head to Vyrin Swiftwind at the Farstrider Lodge.\nOl' Sooty's Head Ol' Sooty\nProvided: Ol' Sooty's Head","desc":"Light! Don't bring things like that into the Lodge... it's unsanitary, unspeakable, un... un... unsanitary!\nJust get it out of here, will you? No one wants to see your bloody little trophy, really!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHunting Ammo Sack Hunting Quiver\nNew in Forever: Hunting Satchel.\nYou will also receive:\nHunting Satchel\nExperience: 1,550","back":"Great job, ‹name›! We really showed him! Here, give me the head and I'll take care of it.","done":"Thanks for helping me out with my little plan, ‹name›. I've been itching for months to get back at that snooty, stuck-up boy, and I'd say we did a pretty good job! Here, have this, you've earned it.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":83.5,"y":65.5,"n":"Daryl the Youngling","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":81.7,"y":64.1,"n":"Vyrin Swiftwind","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"9331":{"id":9331,"t":"Stealing Ironforge's Flame","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 70s instead of 0. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 5,000, 0.99 times as much. No longer rewards Toasted Smorc, Midsummer Sausage, Fire-toasted Bun, Elderberry Pie.","obj":"Return the Flame of Ironforge to the Festival Talespinner.\nFlame of Ironforge\nProvided: Flame of Ironforge","desc":"This flame, stolen from the heart of Ironforge itself, floods you with warmth. This raw power is foreign to you, but the Talespinner might know more...","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Burning Blossom 10 Burning Blossom\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,950","back":"You're practically glowing, ‹race›. What do you have there?","done":"This hearty flame must be from the halls of Ironforge; it's as stalwart as the dwarves themselves. A fine catch, ‹name›. If I had the fires of the other cities... ah, but never mind. Here is your payment.\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":21.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.8,"y":34.9,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":73.1,"n":"Festival Talespinner","e":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"99411":{"id":99411,"t":"Kyles gone missing","lv":7,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Ahab Wheathoof at Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore wants you to feed his prized puppy, Kyle the Frenzied.\nFeed Kyle Tender Strider Meat and return to Ahab Wheathoof.\nKyle Fed\nTender Strider Meat","desc":"Help, ‹name›! My prized puppy, Kyle, has run away! I just know he's running around Bloodhoof Village, lost and hungry.\nWill you find him and feed him? Once he eats he will settle down and come home.\nTo feed him you will need to find food. His favorite meal is tender strider meat. Just venture east and you should find plenty of striders. Hunt one down and take its succulent meat to Kyle. When you see Kyle in town, put the meat down and he is sure to come to you.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.2,"y":57.6,"n":"Ahab Wheathoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"771":{"id":771,"t":"Rite of Vision","lv":7,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 2 Well Stones and 2 Ambercorn and bring them back to Zarlman Two-Moons in Bloodhoof Village.\n2 Well Stone Well Stone , Razorlash 5 %\n2 Ambercorn Ambercorn","desc":"In order to pass through the Rite of Vision, you must gather the reagents needed to make the Water of the Seers.\nI will need well stones, which can be found around the water wells in Mulgore. With those I will combine Ambercorn, which fall beneath the mighty trees in our land.\nThese reagents contain magical elements, and when brewed and consumed before the tribal fire, will cause you to encounter a vision. Follow it, and it will lead you to the next step of this holy quest.","rew":"Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Once you have gathered enough well stones from around the water wells and Ambercorn from beneath the trees, I will prepare the Water of the Seers for you.","done":"I see you have learned to gather from our sacred land, ‹name›. It will take but a moment for me to brew the Water of the Seers.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":61.2,"n":"Zarlman Two-Moons","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9091":{"id":9091,"t":"Dreamwalker Handguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreamwalker Handguards if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Handguards, 8 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 5 Cured Rugged Hides and 1 Nexus Crystal.\nDesecrated Handguards\n8 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n5 Cured Rugged Hide\nNexus Crystal","desc":"Many heroes fell in the last war and many continue to perish at the hands of the Scourge to this day. From the corpses of the fallen, the armor is stripped and taken back to Naxxramas to be used for unknown purposes.\nRecover the desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps and supply to me the other material components I require and I will craft Dreamwalker armor.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreamwalker Handguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The material cost is high, but soon forgotten.","done":"Your Dreamwalker Handguards are ready, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"7491":{"id":7491,"t":"For All To See","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out Overlord Runthak in the Valley of Strength.","desc":"Overlord Runthak awaits your arrival in the Valley of Strength.\n<Thrall salutes you.>\nDo not keep your public waiting, hero.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOnyxia Blood Talisman Dragonslayer's Signet Onyxia Tooth Pendant\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Choose your reward and let the celebration of your glorious victory begin.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":51.7,"y":75.5,"n":"Overlord Runthak","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"9011":{"id":9011,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Mokvar your Coif of Elements and Vest of Elements.\nCoif of Elements Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nVest of Elements General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"A truly amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoif of The Five Thunders Vest of The Five Thunders\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Elements pieces in exchange for your new Coif and Vest of The Five Thunders","done":"I will truly miss you, ‹name›. There is a debt that I owe you, which I may never be able to repay.\nEnjoy your new head and chest armor. May it protect you for a long time to come, and help you to achieve even greater honor!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1651":{"id":1651,"t":"The Tome of Valor","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defend Daphne Stilwell from the Defias attack.\nNeither of your spirits must be released from their mortal coils if you wish to succeed.\nAfter you are successful, speak to Daphne Stilwell again.","desc":"Now, they'll be coming again soon, I'd wager, so get yourself ready.\nI've got myself a gun in the house. I'll grab it and be ready to help you out, but for the most part, you're on your own.\nI've no idea how many they'll send, but I'm sure it'll be more than the few they sent earlier.\nAsk the Light for whatever blessings you can because... did you hear that? I think they're coming.\nWe make our stand near the house!","rew":"Experience: 1,000","back":"We'll make our stand at the house!","done":"We've done it, ‹name›! Thank you for your help. You were truly amazing out there. I never thought a ‹class› could handle so many enemies at once.\nYou've truly shown bravery in the face of overwhelming odds.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":41.7,"y":89.2,"n":"Daphne Stilwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5651":{"id":5651,"t":"In Favor of Darkness","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Dark Cleric Beryl in Tirisfal Glades.","desc":"There are many lessons that the Forsaken have learned through experience--things that some races can only begin to fathom. And although our path lies in darkness, you will find that a great many things rely on both the light and the dark. Your lessons shall teach you to use both... and with discretion. But heed my words: never forget we were forged in corruption and left to rot like so much carrion. The Darkness is our home.\nSeek out Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill when you're ready to learn more.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"Finally, you've arrived. Your faith alone will not allow you to pass the trials before you, young one. A sense of urgency and some ambition will help too.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31.1,"y":66,"n":"Dark Cleric Duesten","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.6,"y":52.2,"n":"Dark Cleric Beryl","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"79731":{"id":79731,"t":"The troll scroll","lv":35,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Solve the riddle of the scroll. Once you've done that, Hemet Nesingwary might like to hear the tale.\nLearn: Solve the riddle","desc":"<The ancient glyphs resolve into words before your eyes.>\nWhen Zul'Kunda's fountain runs with the waters of the holy spring, the gods grant their blessing.","done":"A magic fountain hidden in the jungle? What a story, ‹name›!\nThat gives me an idea for another chapter in my book! Let's see, where did I put that manuscript...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"131":{"id":131,"t":"Delivering Daffodils","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Darcy the Daffodil Bouquet.\nDaffodil Bouquet\nProvided: Daffodil Bouquet","desc":"Here is your bouquet. I chose Daffodils for you. They're my favorite!","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Sauteed Sunfish\nExperience: 270","back":"Hello again, ‹name›. Did Parker like the lunch I sent him?","done":"Oh, those are lovely! I can't wait to put them in some water!\nBut...these are Martie's favorite flowers. Parker didn't have you go to that jealous vixen for this bouquet, did he? You didn't tell her who they were for, did you? If you did, then it wouldn't surprise me if she poisoned them.\nOh, but it's not your fault. Thank you, and here's your meal.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":16.8,"y":46.3,"n":"Martie Jainrose","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.5,"y":44.3,"n":"Darcy","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"4771":{"id":4771,"t":"Dawn's Gambit","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Place Dawn's Gambit in the Viewing Room of the Scholomance. Defeat Vectus, then return to Betina Bigglezink.\nVectus slain in Scholomance\nProvided: Dawn's Gambit","desc":"I've placed Dawn's Gambit in the container you brought to us, the one that held the dragon eggs. Your job is to bring it deep within the Scholomance.\nThe undead mage Vectus leads a team of scourge scholars... place Dawn's Gambit in their chamber, called the \"viewing room.\" It will then react with the undead found there and, with a little luck, destroy them!\nAfter that, defeating Vectus shouldn't be a problem. Right?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWindreaper Dancing Sliver\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Remember, ‹name› - we must be tolerant yet rigid in our beliefs!","done":"You did it! Vectus is defeated! And Dawn's Gambit... did it work?\nHm... maybe my device wasn't the success I had hoped, but I'm glad you were able to handle things anyway. Well done, ‹name›!\nThe Argent Dawn, and the good people of Azeroth, are in your debt.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":49.9,"n":"Betina Bigglezink","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"4451":{"id":4451,"t":"The Key to Freedom","lv":47,"min":43,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search Searing Gorge and find a use for the Grimesilt Outhouse Key you have found.\nGrimesilt Outhouse Key Dark Iron Lookout 3 % , Dark Iron Sentry 3 % , Dark Iron Taskmaster 3 % , Dark Iron Slaver 3 % and 1 more\nProvided: Grimesilt Outhouse Key","desc":"The small brass key looks simple enough.. The only thing that seems to make it stand out are some words scratched into the head of it:\n\"Dark Iron Outhouse - Do Not Duplicate.\"\nYou have no idea what it means or what it will lead to.","rew":"Experience: 5,250","back":"*cough*\nWho is it? Can't ya see I'm busy?","done":"Well, I'll be! How in tarnation!? You found the key! I knew them blasted Dark Irons were hiding it after they locked me in here! Thank ya so much, ‹name›. You're the greatest! Now, just turn the key and let ol' Locheed outta here!","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":65.6,"y":62.2,"n":"Wooden Outhouse","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8771":{"id":8771,"t":"Target: Hive'Ashi Sandstalkers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 30 Hive'Ashi Sandstalkers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing II in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing II\nHive'Ashi Sandstalker slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing II","desc":"As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations. You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Ashi where your primary target will consist of Hive'Ashi sandstalkers.\nReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something to tell me, ‹class›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. Your part in the attack on Hive'Ashi has been noted.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"451":{"id":451,"t":"A Recipe For Death","lv":18,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Wise Gauntlets.","obj":"Bring 6 samples of Lake Creeper Moss, 6 samples of Lake Skulker Moss and a Hardened Tumor to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.\n6 Lake Skulker Moss Elder Lake Skulker 60 % , Lake Skulker 60 %\n6 Lake Creeper Moss Elder Lake Creeper 60 % , Lake Creeper 60 %\nHardened Tumor Vile Fin Tidecaller 5 % , Vile Fin Shorecreeper 5 % , Vile Fin Lakestalker 5 % , Vile Fin Oracle 5 % and 2 more","desc":"According to Berard's Journal the moss from Lake Skulkers and Creepers might prove useful for our quest to brew a new plague. Those beasts dwell on the islands in Lake Lordamere to the east.\nHe also mentions a very rare Hardened Tumor that he discovered on a Vile Fin murloc. Apparently the tumor is so rare Berard was only able to obtain one.\nCollect samples of the moss as well as the rare hardened tumor and take them to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nNightglow Concoction Acidproof Cloak Wise Gauntlets\nNew in Forever: Wise Gauntlets.\nYou will also receive:\nElixir of Minor Fortitude Swiftness Potion\nExperience: 2,050\n+200 reputation with Undercity","back":"What brings you back to the Undercity, ‹name›?","done":"Such a blow to the Royal Apothecary Society to lose Berard. But through your hard work and Apothecary Renferrel's diligent research Berard's studies will still be useful to The Dark Lady's plight.\nWe are on the cusp of something great here, ‹name›. If you were not so skilled in the ways of combat I would try to recruit you for membership in the Society.\nSilverpine Forest Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":48.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"79091":{"id":79091,"t":"Archmage antonidas the unabridged autobiography","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Archmage Antonidas: The Unabridged Autobiography","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nArchmage Antonidas: The Unabridged Autobiography (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. You say this is from the Ironforge library? ...I'm sure they won't miss it.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1091":{"id":1091,"t":"Kaela's Update","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Venture Co. Letters to Kaela Shadowspear.\nVenture Co. Letters Venture Co. Documents\nProvided: Venture Co. Letters","desc":"‹name›, take these letters to Kaela. I'm sure she'll want to know about this. Or at least the Sentinels will.\nMake sure you tell her how successful we were and how we couldn't have done it without a little bit of magic.","rew":"Experience: 180\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Yes, ‹name›? What can I do for you?","done":"This is interesting indeed.\nYou and Gaxim have done very well, ‹name›. Thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.9,"y":66.8,"n":"Kaela Shadowspear","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"97331":{"id":97331,"t":"Zimmixs great escape","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Escort Zimmix Sputterspark away from the Ruins of Zul'Kunda then tell Wharfmaster Lozgil in Booty Bay of your successful rescue.\nEscort Zimmix Sputterspark to safety","desc":"Wait, wait, don't go yet!\nI know I said I just needed the key but... well, they caught me once, they could do it again, right? I'm just one goblin, and there's hundreds of trolls around here!\nYou've already put enough of a dent in their numbers to get this key, so it should be easy enough to stand guard while we mosey on out of here, huh?","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Quest ID 97331\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 35, 5,500 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Where's the Key?\nBring the Primitive Key obtained from the trolls at the Ruins of Zul'kunda in Stranglethorn Vale to Zimmix Sputterspark.\n2,750 XP\n2 [ 35 ] Zimmix's Great Escape this quest\nEscort Zimmix Sputterspark away from the Ruins of Zul'Kunda then tell Wharfmaster Lozgil in Booty Bay of your successful rescue.\n2,750 XP","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"611":{"id":611,"t":"The Curse of the Tides","lv":40,"min":32,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy the Altar of the Tides with Catelyn's Blade, kill Gazban and bring the Stone of the Tides and Catelyn's Blade back to Baron Revilgaz.\nStone of the Tides Gazban\nCatelyn's Blade \"Pretty Boy\" Duncan\nProvided: Catelyn's Blade","desc":"So you're looking for an altar of some sort? Well, I'm no expert on troll ruins like my father, but I have heard about a sunken troll city out near that island you're looking for. Maybe you should try there.\nYou got my knife back for me, so I guess you can borrow it... but I want it back when you're done!","rew":"You will receive:\nRobe of Crystal Waters\nExperience: 3,150\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Have you retrieved the Stone of the Tides for me, ‹name›? I've already cleared out a space and purchased a fine stand for it.","done":"Amazing! The Stone of Tides! It shall have a place of prominence in my collection of ancient troll artifacts. Did you see how it almost seems as though a tide is trapped within its surface? Magnificent!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.3,"y":77.5,"n":"Catelyn the Blade","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":76.9,"n":"Baron Revilgaz","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"5251":{"id":5251,"t":"The Archivist","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stratholme and find Archivist Galford of the Scarlet Crusade. Destroy him and burn down the Scarlet Archive.\nArchivist Galford slain in Stratholme\nArchive Burned in Stratholme","desc":"Anything taken to an extreme is hazardous to our world, ‹name›. Take for example, the Scarlet Crusade. Do you believe that their blind zealotry serves a greater good? How many innocents have they destroyed in the name of the Light?\nBlasphemers, one and all!\nOne in particular interests me, though; the Archivist Galford of Stratholme: A man that watches over the Crusade's most valued documents. Destroy him and burn down his archives! Should you succeed, return to me and be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Remember, ‹name› - we must be tolerant yet rigid in our beliefs!","done":"Outstanding, ‹name›! Years of intelligence, lost! The Scarlet Crusade will surely feel this blow in the coming weeks.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":50.1,"n":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"931":{"id":931,"t":"The Shimmering Frond","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Shimmering Frond to Denalan at Lake Al'Ameth\nShimmering Frond\nProvided: Shimmering Frond","desc":"The fronds on this plant shimmer in the forest light, giving it a twisting, pulsing aura.\nYou believe that Denalan would want a specimen of this.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"You have something for me?","done":"Where did you get this? I haven't seen a plant like this since a sojourn I made to the Swamp of Sorrows... decades ago! It's amazing that a specimen made its way to Teldrassil. And it's grown to such a size!\nThank you, ‹name›. Forgive my shortness of words, but there is a test I would like to perform on this frond...","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":34.6,"y":28.8,"n":"Strange Fronded Plant","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":60.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Denalan","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"851":{"id":851,"t":"Verog the Dervish","lv":18,"min":11,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Verog's Head to Regthar Deathgate, west of the Crossroads.\nVerog's Head Verog the Dervish","desc":"The centaur Verog the Dervish wanders the Barrens, and will be difficult to find. But he is based at the centaur command tent at the Stagnant Oasis to the southeast. It may be possible to draw him to you.\nTravel to the Stagnant Oasis to the southeast and attack centaur near the command tent. It will be dangerous, but if you can kill enough centaur then they should raise an alarm. And Verog will come.\nBring me his head and I will place it with Barak Kodobane's.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,000\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Did you find Verog, ‹name›?","done":"Very good. You must have really stirred up those centaur -- our guards spotted activity down near the Stagnant Oasis, which was probably you.\nYou should be proud of your deed, ‹name›. There is much bravery in you.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.3,"y":28.4,"n":"Regthar Deathgate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"371":{"id":371,"t":"At War With The Scarlet Crusade","lv":10,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Executor Zygand in Brill has commissioned you to slay Captain Vachon and 5 Scarlet Friars.\nCaptain Vachon slain\nScarlet Friar slain : 0/ 5","desc":"We are still at war and the Scarlet Crusade grows in strength. The report Executor Arren sent me indicates Scarlet Crusaders have been raiding from the ruined tower in southeastern Tirisfal near the Balnir Farmstead under the command of Captain Vachon.\nKill Vachon along with 5 Scarlet Friars. It should prove to be a devastating blow to the Crusade!","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I see you have returned but your task is not complete. Perhaps you are at ease with the mere humans interfering with The Dark Lady's plan? Or perhaps you can heed the call of duty and slay Captain Vachon and his band of Scarlet Friars!","done":"Captain Vachon's death will slow down the Scarlet Crusade's advancement in Tirisfal quite a bit. But other threats loom.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.6,"y":51.8,"n":"Executor Zygand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4291":{"id":4291,"t":"The Scent of Lar'korwi","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Ravasaur Pheromone Glands to Torwa Pathfinder near the entrance to Un'Goro Crater.\n2 Ravasaur Pheromone Gland Lar'korwi Mate","desc":"I'm actually surprised he has not come for you yet, ‹name›. But all is well, for I have a final plan that will bring the monster to us.\nBeing the dominant male gives Lar'korwi rights to breed with any female he chooses--and he chooses many of them. You'll find many ravasaur eggs to the west of here. Get close to them and you should provoke an attack by his mates. The females produce an awful smell from a gland in their heads that allow males to know they are ready to breed. Bring me two of those glands.","rew":"Experience: 5,250","back":"Be careful, ‹name›. Getting close to any of nest of eggs surely will provoke the mothers... even if you've already secured a gland from one. The mothers can be just as deadly as Lar'korwi himself when they fight to protect their young. But, if you are successful, then we shall have a definitive way of bringing Lar'korwi out from hiding.","done":"Ah, fine specimens, ‹name›. The two pieces you've found should be perfect for baiting Lar'korwi into the open. I cannot wait to see the outcome of your fight with the monster. He is a massive thing with claws as sharp as the finest blades. You will look into his eyes and you will know death.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":71.6,"y":76,"n":"Torwa Pathfinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"97891":{"id":97891,"t":"Prompt potion runner","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Unstable Potion to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium within the time limit.\nSpeak to Doctor Martin Felben","desc":"You! Quickly, I need you to bring this potion across the slime canal to Doctor Martin Felben in the Apothecarium!\nIt has a very limited shelf life, and no I can't go myself, my knees rattle and pop out if I attempt to run.\nJust another lovely side effect of undeath, apparently.\nBut we're wasting time! Here, take this and go!\n<Alessandro makes a shooing motion.>","rew":"Money: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+150 reputation with Undercity","done":"Ah, marvelous! I had been waiting for Alessandro's potion to arrive. The last six he sent destabilized along the way, but you've made it just in time!\nHere, take this for your effort. That is all for now, unless you have other business with me?\nIf not, remove yourself so I may continue my experiments unhindered.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":58.2,"y":55.2,"n":"Alessandro Luca","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":46.6,"y":74.4,"n":"Doctor Martin Felben","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1491":{"id":1491,"t":"Smart Drinks","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,650 experience instead of 1,350, 1.96 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Bring 6 portions of Wailing Essence to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.\n6 Wailing Essence Nightmare Ectoplasm , Evolving Ectoplasm , Devouring Ectoplasm","desc":"Ok, so the raptor horns didn't work so well. But that's all right -- no one got rich on their first try! And besides, I think I found something that'll work even better in my smart drinks!\nThere is a substance called Wailing Essence, and I think it is the cause of the strange plants and animals in the Barrens. Get me some and I'll try it in my drink!\nI heard the essence gathers in ectoplasmic creatures in the Wailing Caverns to the west. Hunt those creatures and gather the essence.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Where is my wailing essence?","done":"Great, you got it! I can't wait to try it out. This is going to make me a fortune, I just know it!\nThank you, ‹name›. Take this, and after I'm rich I'll send you more, I promise!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.4,"y":37.6,"n":"Mebok Mizzyrix","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wailing-caverns"]},"3091":{"id":3091,"t":"Simple Note","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Simple Note and speak to Harutt Thunderhorn in Camp Narache.\nSimple Note\nProvided: Simple Note","desc":"Just a moment ago a messenger was looking for you, ‹name›. I believe she was sent by the warrior trainer Harutt. If this note is from Harutt, I wouldn't take long in reading it's contents.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Ah, at last, you've arrived, warrior. I did not lie in my note, ‹name›. We are a special breed also, not unlike the druids or shamans of our tribe. You are just as important. We are the ones called upon to defend our borders, to hunt the centaur, and to go to war.","done":"Each of us plays a role in our tribe. Each of us must also go through all the same rites. Do not ever let your pride tell you otherwise.\nI remain here to train new warriors that seek the glory of battle and who follow the ways of our oldest ancestors. When you feel ready, come back to me and I will do what I can to train you further. Go with the tribe's blessing, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.5,"y":77.5,"n":"Grull Hawkwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":43.7,"y":76.7,"n":"Harutt Thunderhorn","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8291":{"id":8291,"t":"Vanquish the Invaders!","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Horde, obtain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and return to Sentinel Farsong at the Silverwing Grove.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"Beyond this tunnel you will find a field of strife and turmoil, young ‹class›. The Horde continue to decimate our sacred forest, cutting down the evergreen foliage to power their machines of war.\nEnter Warsong Gulch and defend Silverwing Hold. Push back the invading Horde forces!\nDo this, and earn a talisman of merit. Bring me such a talisman, ‹name›, and I shall reward you.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\nLevel 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Dwarf, Night Elf, Gnome Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8291","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"211":{"id":211,"t":"Alas, Andorhal","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Araj's Phylactery Shard to Commander Ashlam Valorfist at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\nAraj's Phylactery Shard Araj's Phylactery","desc":"Alas, the time to attack Andorhal and drive out the lich that controls it is upon us!\nInside the ruins of the city is where the lich - Araj the Summoner - holds dominion. He is guarded by numerous Scourge surrounding the remains of city's center, and his personal retinue of guardians attached to him directly is formidable. You will need numerous allies to even stand a chance of facing him successfully.\nDestroy Araj, ‹name›, and bring me a shard from his phylactery as proof!","rew":"You will receive:\nMark of Resolution\nExperience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Alliance\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Your task has been given to you, ‹name›. Do you have a shard from the lich's phylactery as proof of the task being accomplished?","done":"You've done it! Araj... the lich is finally defeated!\nYou've done a tremendous service to the Alliance on this day, ‹name›. Your bravery and perseverance are a testament to what it means to be a true hero. Please - accept this as a token for all to see and know that you have delivered the Alliance a victory for the ages!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"51":{"id":51,"t":"Sweet Amber","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Sycamore Branch to Grimbooze Thunderbrew.\nA Sycamore Branch Cursed Sycamore","desc":"Not yet filtered but freshly distilled\nLike unseeded land waiting there tilled.\nNext I will fashion our pile of charcoal\nDeliver a sycamore branch, that is your next goal.","rew":"Money: 1 25 1 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,650","back":"An encore? Why for you, anything!\nNot yet filtered but freshly distilled\nLike unseeded land waiting there tilled.\nNext I will fashion our pile of charcoal\nDeliver a sycamore branch, that is your next goal.","done":"Hiccup! Ho ho!\nWestfall Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":44.6,"y":80.3,"n":"Grimbooze Thunderbrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"98291":{"id":98291,"t":"Death to the dragonmaw","lv":30,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 8 Dragonmaw Reclaimers, 5 Dragonmaw Soulbinders, and 3 Dragonmaw Infiltrators in Dragonmaw Retreat for Howin Kindfeather.\nDragonmaw Reclaimer slain : 0/ 8\nDragonmaw Soulbinder slain : 0/ 5\nDragonmaw Infiltrator slain : 0/ 3","desc":"I plan tae get back into Grim Batol and reclaim it for the Wildhammers, ‹name›. Or at least learn a thing or two.\nDon't look at me like that, now. I know the risks. I don't intend tae go in hammer swingin', ye know.\nRegardless, I'll need your help first. The Dragonmaw orcs march as we speak. They're all up an' down the Dragonmaw Retreat, where the red dragons routed them before.\nI need you tae thin their numbers before I have any chance of gettin' close. Ye can't miss 'em if you follow the road east.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.4,"y":42,"n":"Howin Kindfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"87491":{"id":87491,"t":"Spark of freedom","lv":32,"min":27,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Escort the captive fire elemental out of Dun Modr and to its freedom.\nEscort the fire elemental out of Dun Modr","desc":"Sss! The foul Dark Irons have summoned me and kept me caged next to their petty fire pit!\nFire must run wild, run free! Release me! Must escape! Must BURN!\nNo Dark Iron is safe! Burn them to the ground! Burn their black powder! Burn their fortress, their fuses, their folly!\nLet me out and I will BURN THEM ALL!","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":45.7,"y":16.6,"n":"Captive Fire Elemental","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.8,"y":18.1,"n":"Roggo Harlbarrow","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"8051":{"id":8051,"t":"The Eye of Zuldazar","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"The Eye of Zuldazar","rew":"You will receive:\nThe Eye of Zuldazar\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Welcome ‹class›. The Eye of Zuldazar pulses with energy. You are ready to take the next step. Hand me the talisman and I shall perform the imbue.","done":"Continue in your battle against the Soulflayer and his minions, ‹name›. He must never be permitted to leave the confines of Zul'Gurub.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});